On Wed, Jan 26, 2022 at 03:58:28PM -0800, Mat Martineau wrote:
> On Tue, 25 Jan 2022, Geliang Tang wrote:
> 
> > Add a flag infinite_sent in struct mptcp_subflow_context, to make sure
> > only one infinite map is sent.
> 
> Could you explain more about the extra infinite mappings you mention in the
> cover letter? Maybe share a pcap?

Hi Mat,

As I said in the cover letter, I got two issues when running the MP_FAIL
testcases:

 - send too many infinite maps, the data translation was cease.
 - the infinite map may be lost, it wasn't received.

I just reproduced issue #1 twice, and all the pcaps and logs are attached.

Issue #2 only happened when this adding infinite_sent patch is applied.
When only one infinite map is sent, the reset will happen.

These issues are easy to reproduce.

Run the MP_FAIL testcases with this change, issue #2 happened:

'''
diff --git a/net/mptcp/subflow.c b/net/mptcp/subflow.c
index 4d8574f5ad2b..606e95fa1c9b 100644
--- a/net/mptcp/subflow.c
+++ b/net/mptcp/subflow.c
@@ -1177,7 +1177,7 @@ static bool subflow_check_data_avail(struct sock *ssk)
                                while ((skb = skb_peek(&ssk->sk_receive_queue)))
                                        sk_eat_skb(ssk, skb);
                        } else {
-                               subflow->infinite_expect = 1;
+                               subflow->infinite_expect = 0;
                        }
                        WRITE_ONCE(subflow->data_avail, MPTCP_SUBFLOW_NODATA);
                        return true;
'''

And run the MP_FAIL testcases with this change, issue #1 happened:

'''
diff --git a/net/mptcp/protocol.h b/net/mptcp/protocol.h
index ddaa86acadce..0dbced92e1ec 100644
--- a/net/mptcp/protocol.h
+++ b/net/mptcp/protocol.h
@@ -903,7 +903,7 @@ static inline bool mptcp_check_infinite_map(struct mptcp_subflow_context *subflo
        mpext = skb ? mptcp_get_ext(skb) : NULL;
        if (mpext && mpext->infinite_map &&
            !subflow->infinite_sent) {
-               subflow->infinite_sent = 1;
+               subflow->infinite_sent = 0;
                return true;
        }
'''

Thanks,
-Geliang

